# No Comprehensive Documentation

Do NOT create comprehensive markdown documentation files unless explicitly requested by the user.

## What NOT to Create

- ❌ API documentation files (API_INTEGRATION.md, API_DOCS.md, etc.)
- ❌ Implementation summary files (IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md)
- ❌ Quick start guides (QUICK_START_*.md)
- ❌ Architecture diagrams in markdown (AUTH_FLOW_DIAGRAM.md, etc.)
- ❌ Checklist documents (BACKEND_CHECKLIST_*.md)
- ❌ Any other comprehensive .md files

## When to Create Documentation

ONLY create documentation files when:
- The user explicitly asks for documentation
- The user specifically requests a README or markdown file
- It's a required project file (like package.json, tsconfig.json, etc.)

## What to Do Instead

- Focus on code implementation
- Add inline code comments where necessary
- Provide brief explanations in chat responses
- Keep documentation minimal and in-code
